bound-lock/1 about="head asks to found your place at {dir} — a root key made in your keychain, reads bounded, nothing it may write — to connect {source} to it from {document}, compiled once and pinned, to prove access to it where its document declares how, on head's page or at its provider, and to let head read {source} until {until}: no read of it asks again before then, and anything that is not a read still does. Say yes only to all of it; a place elsewhere, named as you like, can be founded instead." at=policy:head/words/0.1.7 by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/elicit-first-run value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="head asks to use {origin}: a place of its own at {dir}, read-only — nothing that is not a read is ever called there — its document found where {origin} publishes it and compiled, and reads granted until {until}. Say yes only to this." at=policy:head/surface/0.1.1g by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/elicit-use value=lock
